                <pb facs="0392" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/2008: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-30T13:00:00-05:00">November 30, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>324. The American Embassy at Nanking reports that there remain at Nanking about
                    40 Americans including 5 members of the Embassy staff who are at the Embassy.
                    The U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> is also at Nanking. It is
                    understood that a number of Americans together with a number of other nationals
                    are being accommodated on Jardine Matheson and Company’s hulk which lies 4 miles
                    up river from the Nanking Bund.</p>
                <p>Please bring the above to the attention of the Japanese Foreign Office with the
                    request that the appropriate Japanese military and naval authorities be promptly
                    notified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
